# earlyoom: last-ditch guard against thrash-freezes. Kills one process, only when RAM
# and zram swap are both nearly gone (-m 5: below 5% free RAM, -s 10: below 10% free swap).
# --prefer: things that die gracefully (browser content processes, JVM/Gradle daemons).
# --avoid:  browser parents, the desktop session, audio, the charging daemon.
# systemd-oomd is not used: with every app in one session scope it kills the whole desktop.
# Word-split by systemd: no spaces or quotes inside patterns.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 8,4 -s 100,100 -r 0 -n --prefer (^|/)(Isolated.Web.Co|Web.Content|java|kotlin.*|gradle.*)$ --avoid (^|/)(zen|zen-bin|firefox|Hyprland|qs|quickshell|sddm|Xwayland|pipewire|wireplumber|book4-charge|agent-host|systemd.*|dbus.*)$"
